The datasheet lists one part (`SO-SFP-155M-L160D`), with protocol support `FE, STM1/OC3` and bit rates `100 to 155Mbps`; the overview ties **100M Fast Ethernet** to 100 Mbps and **155 Mbps SDH/SONET** to STM-1/OC-3. Transmit wavelength is **1480–1580 nm** (same module for all services). Receiver **1260–1600 nm** is a common Rx sensitivity range, not a separate selectable mode—so service modes use the Tx band. No penalties or amplified/unamplified splits appear in the source.

